add('selection8',6.5,'Geometry',['tangency','cyclic quadrilaterals'],'Identify an initial tangent, then use the equal-distance condition and directed angles to prove collinearity.','selection',8,r'In acute $ABC$ with $AC>AB$, let $O$ be its circumcentre and $D\in BC$. The perpendicular to $BC$ through $D$ meets $AO,AC,AB$ at $W,X,Y$. Put $Z=(AXY)\cap(ABC)$, $Z\ne A$. If $OW=OD$, prove $DZ$ tangent to $(AXY)$.',page=21)
