add('selection10',5.5,'Number theory',['recurrences','periodicity'],'Bound the sequence, prove unique predecessors, and trace a returning one backwards through powers.','selection',10,r'For coprime integers $a,d>1$, set $x_1=1$ and $x_{k+1}=x_k/a$ when $a\mid x_k$, otherwise $x_k+d$. Find the largest $n\ge0$ for which some term is divisible by $a^n$.',page=26)
